Why the Canon Exists
R2D changes the order in which scientific objects and laws are interpreted. A focused paper on muscle, thermodynamics, quantum mechanics, gravity, or biology cannot reproduce the entire framework every time.
The Canon therefore provides the common source beneath those narrower developments.
It preserves:

the primitive definitions and mathematical architecture of R2D;
the derivations and logical dependencies connecting those definitions;
physical mappings and empirical calibrations;
applications across scientific domains;
failed routes, qualifications, and unresolved questions;
and the subsequent addenda through which the framework continues to develop.

The Canon has three primary roles.

Archive
The Canon preserves the development of R2D as completely as possible at a particular stage of the program.
Formal versions are deposited on Zenodo so that earlier formulations remain permanently available, citable, and distinguishable from later developments.


Authoritative Source
The Canon is the authoritative mathematical source for R2D.
The explanatory pages on R2DScience.org are designed to make the framework easier to navigate, understand, and use. Applications isolate particular scientific problems. Essays provide interpretation and commentary.
When a question depends on the formal definitions, assumptions, derivations, or logical status of an R2D claim, the Canon is the reference document.


AI Source Corpus
The Canon is also designed to be used by artificial intelligence.
R2D introduces a mathematical language that differs from the physical ontologies normally used in science. An AI given only a short description will tend to translate that language immediately back into familiar concepts such as particles, forces, fields, trajectories, energy, space, or time.
The Canon provides enough of the internal mathematical structure for an AI to remain inside the R2D framework long enough to interrogate it.
It can therefore be supplied to an LLM as a source corpus and used to:

reconstruct an R2D argument;
test a proposed implication;
search for internal contradictions;
compare R2D with an established scientific theory;
analyze a scientific law or paradox;
and explore whether a scientific problem changes when its inherited physical ontology is removed.

The goal is not for an AI to accept R2D.
The goal is to give AI enough of the mathematics to run it.
